\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.2}{\ignorespaces Source ablation: chained out-of-sample value of the same DRL design with three input sets (three seeds each), compared with the ETF, equal weight, and the ridge forecast.}}{16}{figure.caption.11}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.3}{\ignorespaces Five starter stocks: chained out-of-sample value over the seven validation years for the five algorithms at 300{,}000 timesteps, with the ETF, equal weight and the ridge forecast. Lines are seed means and bands the range across five seeds.}}{17}{figure.caption.13}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.4}{\ignorespaces Point-in-time SET50: chained out-of-sample value over the seven validation years for the DRL agent with traded-value slots, with sticky slots, and with the shared-weight actor, and for the baselines. Each year uses models trained only on earlier years; bands show the range across three seeds.}}{25}{figure.caption.16}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.5}{\ignorespaces Point-in-time SET50: chained out-of-sample value of the seed ensemble with the no-trade band for three input sets: technical and SET50 market inputs, the same plus the BOT policy rate, and the same plus the daily macro proxies, with the ETF and equal weight. Everything except the inputs is identical.}}{26}{figure.caption.17}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.6}{\ignorespaces Point-in-time SET50: chained out-of-sample value of the shared-weight design trained for 100{,}000 and 300{,}000 timesteps (five seeds each), as single models and as a seed ensemble with the no-trade band, with the ETF and equal weight. Bands show the range across seeds.}}{28}{figure.caption.19}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.7}{\ignorespaces Point-in-time SET50, test years 2023--2024: chained value of the locked DRL design (the seed ensemble with the no-trade band) and of its single models (mean of three seeds; the band shows their range), with the ETF and equal weight. Each year uses models trained only on earlier years; net of costs.}}{32}{figure.caption.21}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.8}{\ignorespaces Point-in-time SET50, sealed holdout 2025 to 4 November 2026: chained value of the locked DRL design (the seed ensemble with the no-trade band) and of its single models (mean of three seeds; the band shows their range), with the ETF and equal weight. Each fold uses models trained only on earlier years; net of costs.}}{33}{figure.caption.23}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.9}{\ignorespaces Point-in-time SET50, validation 2016--2022, checks after the holdout: chained value of the seed ensemble with the no-trade band for each input set (five seeds each), with the ETF and equal weight. ``Technical + ETF market (locked)'' is the locked design. Each year uses models trained only on earlier years; net of costs.}}{36}{figure.caption.27}%
